    specialisms: ["Breast surgical oncology", "Adjuvant and neoadjuvant trials", "Genomic risk assays", "Cooperative-group leadership"],
    tldr: "Surgeon who chairs the NRG Oncology breast committee and co-led the KATHERINE and B-42 trials.", summary: "Eleftherios Mamounas (Orlando Health) chairs the NRG Oncology Breast Committee and was NSABP protocol chair for B-42 (extended letrozole) and co-chair of KATHERINE, which established adjuvant T-DM1 for residual disease after neoadjuvant therapy. He has led work using the 21-gene assay to predict locoregional recurrence and radiotherapy benefit. His current trials test omission of surgery and radiotherapy after excellent neoadjuvant response.",
