    tldr: "The surgeon on CheckMate 816 who showed neoadjuvant immunotherapy does not make lung cancer operations harder.", summary: "Jonathan Spicer led the surgical analyses of CheckMate 816, demonstrating that neoadjuvant nivolumab plus chemotherapy did not delay or complicate surgery and increased the rate of complete resection, which removed a key objection to neoadjuvant immunotherapy. He co-authored the five-year update and leads perioperative surgical research at McGill.",
