    tldr: "Dutch surgeon who leads the PREOPANC trials testing chemotherapy or chemoradiation before pancreatic cancer surgery.", summary: "Marc Besselink (Amsterdam UMC) leads the Dutch Pancreatic Cancer Group and was senior investigator of PREOPANC, the randomised trial showing neoadjuvant chemoradiotherapy improves long-term survival in resectable and borderline resectable pancreatic cancer, and of PREOPANC-2 comparing neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX. He has led the DIPLOMA and LEOPARD trials of minimally invasive pancreatic surgery.",
