    specialisms: ["Urothelial cancer", "Antibody-drug conjugates", "FGFR-targeted therapy", "Immunotherapy"],
    tldr: "Led the early enfortumab vedotin trials and the atezolizumab study that first brought immunotherapy to bladder cancer.", summary: "Jonathan Rosenberg led IMvigor210, the first pivotal study of a PD-L1 inhibitor in urothelial cancer, and EV-201, the trial that won enfortumab vedotin accelerated approval, and was a lead investigator of EV-103 and EV-302. He has also led erdafitinib and other FGFR3-directed studies. He chairs GU oncology at MSKCC and the Alliance GU committee.",
