    tldr: "Surgeon who chairs the German AGO group and led DESKTOP III, proving secondary surgery can extend survival in selected relapsed ovarian cancer.", summary: "Andreas du Bois (Kliniken Essen-Mitte) chairs the AGO ovarian cancer study group, whose trials established carboplatin-paclitaxel as standard and defined the prognostic value of complete cytoreduction. He was principal investigator of DESKTOP III, which showed secondary cytoreductive surgery improves overall survival in AGO-score-positive platinum-sensitive relapse, and of the TRUST trial of primary versus interval surgery.",
