    tldr: "Gynaecologic oncologist who co-led KEYNOTE-826, innovaTV 301 and KEYNOTE-A18, the trials that rebuilt cervical cancer treatment.", summary: "Bradley Monk (GOG Partners) was a lead investigator of GOG 240, which established bevacizumab in advanced cervical cancer, and co-led KEYNOTE-826, innovaTV 301 (tisotumab vedotin) and KEYNOTE-A18, together the three practice-changing cervical cancer trials of the past five years. He co-leads the GOG Partners industry-collaboration programme and has led ovarian PARP inhibitor trials including ATHENA.",
